  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{y}^2=4 \\mathrm{ax} \\text { and } \\mathrm{x}^2=4 \\mathrm{by}$\n\nEq. of normal to $y^2=4 a x$ and $x^2=4 b y$ \n are $y=m x-2 a m-a m^3$ and $y=m x+2 b+\\frac{b}{m^2}$\n\nFor common normal; $2 \\mathrm{~b}+\\frac{\\mathrm{b}}{\\mathrm{m}^2}+2 \\mathrm{am}+\\mathrm{am}^3=0$\n$\\Rightarrow a m^5+2 a m^3+2 b m^2+b=0$\n\nMax. 5 common normal",
